<title>PORTUGAL: P.Telecom mobile unit Q1 profit up 574 pct.</title>
<headline>P.Telecom mobile unit Q1 profit up 574 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ending March 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     2.66   (up 547 percent)</p>
<p>    Sales		   15.50   (up 108 percent)</p>
<p>Note - TMN-Telefones Moveis Nacionais is owned 100 percent by Portugal Telecom.  </p>
<p>    Cashflow		 4.15   (up 132 percent)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	 3.83</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that the number of clients nearly doubled between January and March, compared with the same period last year, to stand at 370,824.</p>
<p>In the first quarter, new subscriptions totalled 38,561, up 96.5 percent on the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
